{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0t8cgs","slideIndex":1,"text":"Stock prices change for many reasons, so choosing trading rules is difficult. We use historical data to teach a model to recognize patterns. Then we search for rules that balance returns and risk. Finally, we test those rules on later data that the search did not use. The goal is to study the method honestly, including when it performs poorly.\nSource: PROJECT.md and approved research protocol."}
