{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0u27wy","slideIndex":3,"text":"First, we collect historical prices and calculate indicators. LightGBM uses those indicators to estimate the chance of an upward move over the next three trading bars. NSGA-II then searches for entry, exit and risk settings. The simulator applies the resulting rules to later data and includes trading costs. The dashboard helps us inspect returns, losses and individual trades.\nSources: src/predictor.py; src/evolutionary_core.py; src/backtest_engine.py."}
