{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/5oru1cva","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":690,"top":300,"width":510,"height":230},"text":"Improves candidate trading rules\n\nBalances Sharpe ratio and maximum drawdown","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":31,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#172B4D","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/4nyd87up","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":78,"top":590,"width":1130,"height":65},"text":"Sharpe: return relative to variability     Drawdown: largest fall from a peak","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#64748B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/lzfh35","slideIndex":4,"text":"LightGBM learns from past examples and produces a probability estimate. It does not guarantee a future price movement. NSGA-II tries different trading rules and improves them over multiple rounds. It balances two objectives: Sharpe ratio and maximum drawdown. Sharpe describes return relative to variability. Drawdown is the largest fall from a previous portfolio peak. Different candidates offer different tradeoffs.\nSources: src/predictor.py; src/evolutionary_core.py."}
