{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/23imm8","slideIndex":6,"text":"Select a stock, such as Reliance. For a simple demonstration, use forty candidates, fifteen generations and random seed forty-two. Population means the number of candidate rule sets. Generations means how many rounds the optimizer improves them. The seed helps repeat its random choices. Click Run Experiment and inspect the results. This dashboard demonstration uses a single split, unlike the separate rolling research study.\nSources: app.py; src/pipeline.py. Demo40/15/42 versus rolling30/10 with GAseeds42/43/44. Model seed is fixed separately."}
